{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart@navapbc.com","data":{"body":"## Plan review returned BLOCK; the mechanism it challenged was wrong, and measuring it changed the fix\n\nThe review's lead finding was that the failing tests \"already establish a repo-local\n`user.email` via `_git_backed`\", so the proposed fix would re-do what the tests already do.\nThat is correct about what the tests do and decisive about the plan being wrong — but the\nconclusion is not that the fix is redundant. The tests set identity on a **different repo**\nthan the one the check reads.\n\nMeasured:\n\n- `owned_repair_pause` reads `identity._git_email(config.repo_root(...))` — the\n  **repo root** (`_repair_pause.py:117`), which shells `git config user.email` with\n  `cwd=root` (`identity.py:86-102`).\n- `_git_backed` configures `user.email` on the **tmp tracker**\n  (`test_doctor.py:437-448`).\n- The 5 failing tests redirect only `tracker_dir` (lines 518, 567, 655, 697, 733). None\n  redirects `repo_root`.\n\nSo the identity they establish is invisible to the check.\n\nThe second measurement is what makes the scrub load-bearing here:\n\n```\ngit config --local  user.email   -> (empty)\ngit config --global user.email   -> (empty)\nGIT_CONFIG_COUNT=8\ngit config user.email            -> joeoakhart@navapbc.com\n```\n\nLocal and global are both unset in this checkout. The only source of `repo_root` identity is\nthe harness-injected command-scope config — precisely what the scrub removes.\n\n**The 5 tests that redirect `tracker_dir` are exactly the 5 that fail.**\n\nThis also explains why CI is green and this was not caught: a runner with a global\n`user.email` satisfies the `repo_root` lookup whether or not the scrub runs. The defect\nmanifests only where identity is ambient-only.\n\nThe description has been rewritten around this mechanism. The other three findings are\naddressed there: the identity-test oracle is now a self-contained pytest selection rather\nthan a pointer at `985f`'s list, and the new helper is specified as writing repo-local\nconfig to a caller-supplied path with an explicit prohibition on mutating `os.environ` —\nthe review was right that an `os.environ`-mutating helper would re-introduce the exact\nsession-wide leak the scrub exists to remove."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789711265468435001,"uuid":"6abf557b-565e-4424-8e7d-b239ef8e62f5"}